# Production releases (CI/CD)

**Source of truth for production:** push (or merge) to **`main`**. GitHub Actions CD runs quality checks, applies pending `db/migrations/*.sql`, then deploys to Vercel.

## Do

- Ship schema + app together: add a new file under `db/migrations/`, then merge to `main`.
- Prefer GitHub Actions over one-off `vercel --prod` or remote SQL for routine releases.
- Keep GitHub secrets in sync with Vercel Production `DATABASE_URL`.

## Avoid

- Editing shipped migration files (hooks block this; add a new file).
- Relying on Vercel Git auto-deploy for production if CD owns prod (disable Production auto-deploy so migrate-then-deploy stays ordered).
- Pointing local `.env.local` `DATABASE_URL` at production while developing (use Docker or Singapore QA).

